# Coin Inventory server — environment overrides. NONE of these are required.
#
# A normal install needs none: the database builds itself under
# %LOCALAPPDATA%CoinInventory on first run. Copy this file to .env only to
# override something.
#
# Leave a variable commented out rather than empty; an empty value is not absent: `PORT=` parses to NaN rather than 3000, and
# `SPOT_PRICE_BASE_URL=` would send every price request to an empty URL.
#
# Where the database file is. An absolute path, or :memory: for a throwaway
# in-memory database. Read before any platform logic, so it overrides
# everything. Absent: %LOCALAPPDATA%\CoinInventory\coin-inventory.db.
# The test suite sets this to :memory: itself, before db/config.ts is asked
# anything, so running the specs can never touch a real collection.
# COIN_INVENTORY_DB_PATH=

# The folder to keep the default coin-inventory.db in, when only the directory
# should change — "two collections side by side" without having to know the
# file name. Ignored when COIN_INVENTORY_DB_PATH is set.
# Absent: %LOCALAPPDATA%\CoinInventory.
# COIN_INVENTORY_DATA_DIR=

# Port the API listens on. Absent: 3000, which is what start-coin-inventory.ps1
# polls for readiness — change this and you must change the launcher too.
# PORT=3000

# Base URL of the spot-price provider. Absent: the live Yahoo Finance chart
# endpoint. Overridable because the endpoint is
# undocumented, and so tests can use a local stub.
# SPOT_PRICE_BASE_URL=

# Absolute path GET /api/app-info should report as the install folder. Absent:
# the folder found by walking up from the module until a directory contains
# angular.json, which is correct both under tsx and from a compiled dist/. Set
# it only when that answer is wrong — an odd unpack, a symlink, a service.
# APP_BASE_FOLDER=

# The GitHub repository "Help > Report a problem" files issues against. Absent:
# a placeholder URL, and the API reports `repositoryConfigured: false` rather
# than opening a 404 at a user who believes they have been heard.
# SUPPORT_REPO_URL=

# Where support reports are written. Absent: the user's Desktop, falling
# back to their home folder.
# COIN_SUPPORT_OUTPUT_DIR=

# Where log files are written. Absent: server/logs.
# COIN_LOG_DIR=
